                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 2,
                "retweet_count": 3,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Over the 43 days of this shutdown, House Republicans refused to negotiate or even show up in D.C., went out of their way to take food assistance away from millions of Americans to try to pressure Democrats, and made your healthcare more expensive to pay for tax breaks for billionaires. \n\nI just left the floor of the House, where I refused to rubber-stamp the same Republican agenda that got us into this shutdown mess and created a healthcare crisis. My vote reflects my commitment to my constituents. \n\nI won\u2019t stop fighting until this nation treats healthcare as a human right.",
                "text_lang": "en",
